---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About | Joe Fazio"
  description="Joe Fazio: recent Computer Information Systems graduate looking for work across IT."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I'm Joe. I graduated from James Madison University with a degree in Computer
    Information Systems, taken through the College of Business, which mostly
    meant learning to ask what a system is <em>for</em> before arguing about how
    to build it.
  </p>

  <p>
    I'm looking for work across IT: help desk, systems administration, cloud
    support, IT analyst, junior security. That is a wide net and it is
    deliberate. I would rather land somewhere I can be useful early and grow
    sideways than pick a title now and pretend I have been walking toward it the
    whole time.
  </p>

  <h2>What I'm building</h2>

  <p>
    This site, mostly. It's a static site built with Astro, hosted on Cloudflare
    Pages, on a domain whose DNS I manage myself. Every push runs a build in
    GitHub Actions, and nothing reaches the main branch unless that build
    passes. The repository is public, and the decision log is part of it: every
    choice here has a written reason attached, including the ones I got wrong
    the first time and had to go back and fix.
  </p>

  <p>
    I built it this way on purpose. I wanted infrastructure I could explain out
    loud, line by line, rather than a template I clicked into existence.
  </p>
</Layout>
